pfep_description_raw:
The maximum extent of corrosion of a canister at 1000 years has been conservatively estimated (see FEPs 2.4, 2.5, 2.6) at 
		-	1 mm due to corrosion by oxygen;
		-	9 mm due to corrosion by sulphides;
		-	20 mm due to anoxic corrosion by water.
The estimated maximum extent of corrosion by all three processes combined is thus 30 mm in 1000 years, significant uneven corrosion being ruled out (see FEP 2.7), compared with the canister-wall corrosion allowance of 50 mm (see FEP 2.2).  Realistically, actual corrosion rates may be much lower.

