pfep_description_raw:
The beneficial properties of bentonite as a buffer material (swelling, low permeability and sorption properties) may be significantly affected by reactions with cement.  Possible reactions are (DUERDEN 1992):
	 –  zeolitization can only occur at high temperatures (~ 200 ˚C) and therefore unlikely in the Swiss HLW repository design;
	 –  beidillitization - the dissolution of silica from the clay lattice with precipitation resulting in reduced porosity and plasticity;
	 –  ion exchange - substitution of Ca2+ ions from cement for Na+ ions in Na-bentonite, resulting in reduced swelling pressure and plasticity and increased permeability.

Such reactions, even if they occur, cannot be significant in the Swiss HLW repository because there would be only very limited quantities of cementitious material in the HLW panels (see also FEP 4.15).

