pfep_description_raw:
The mineralogy of the LPD is heterogeneous.  The average mineralogy of the water-conducting features differs from that of the undisturbed rock.  The mineralogy varies: 
(i) according to whether the undisturbed rock is a granite or a gneiss; 
(ii) according to the type of water-conducting feature (see FEP 5.2); 
(iii) within a water-conducting feature, between fracture infill, altered wallrock and unaltered wallrock; 
(iv) according to the type of alteration, e.g. high-temperature alteration or argillic alteration.  
The mineralogy of the LPD partially determines the groundwater chemistry (see FEP 5.8).  Both mineralogy and groundwater chemistry influence radionuclide sorption (see FEP 5.9).

The mineralogy of the LPD is assumed to be unperturbed by the presence of the repository.  Mineralogy is taken into account in the selection of sorption parameter values.

